    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0847" n="721" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg721"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5045/278: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-12-22T21:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 22,
                                1925—9 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 22—11:48
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>540. My telegram 538, December 21, 8 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Interested ministers today authorized senior minister to give out to the
                        press tomorrow afternoon, together with announcement of the action taken by
                        the Shanghai Municipal Council, documents referred to in the second
                        paragraph of my telegram 525, December 12, noon. Publication of full texts
                        of reports will follow in due course.<anchor n="37" xml:id="d573-f1"
                        /></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>I have expressed to Cunningham my appreciation of his part in bringing
                        about action by Shanghai Municipal Council in accepting resignations of
                        McEuen and Everson and offering $75,000 solatium to victims or their
                        families. I trust this action brings Shanghai incident to a conclusion as
                        satisfactory as could have been hoped for.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d573-f1" n="37" xml:id="d573-f1-content">
                <p>The Minister in China in despatch No. 430, Jan. 22, 1926, reported that the texts
                    of the reports were to be released to the press by the Senior Minister on
                    January 23 (file No. 893.5045/278).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
